            {
              "id": "glog-aa2ee7d7-68a2-41a0-86cc-af56acf1225d",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe \"Detected Issue with C Function (strlen)\" vulnerability in C++ arises when the `strlen` function is used improperly, potentially leading to buffer overflows or reading beyond the intended memory bounds. This can occur if the input string is not null-terminated or if the function is used without proper bounds checking. Such vulnerabilities can lead to undefined behavior, crashes, or security issues like information disclosure or code execution.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Input Validation**: Always validate input to ensure it is null-terminated before passing it to `strlen`.\n2. **Bounds Checking**: Use safer alternatives like `strnlen` where you can specify the maximum number of characters to read.\n3. **Use Safer Libraries**: Consider using safer string handling libraries that automatically manage memory and prevent overflows.\n4. **Static Analysis Tools**: Employ static analysis tools to detect potential vulnerabilities in your code.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the use of `strlen` with `strnlen` to ensure that the function does not read beyond the intended buffer size.\n\n```cpp\n#include <cstring> // Required for strnlen\n\nsize_t safe_strlen(const char* suffix, size_t max_len) {\n    return strnlen(suffix, max_len);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    const char* suffix = \"example\";\n    size_t max_len = 100; // Define a reasonable maximum length\n    size_t length = safe_strlen(suffix, max_len);\n    // Use length safely\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\n- `<cstring>`: Required for `strnlen`.\n\n### OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-126: Buffer Over-read](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/126.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS140021"
                ]
              }
